# Firestore / Pub-Sub access

- All Firestore reads/writes go through `app/services/` platform-client modules. Department code, tool functions, and route handlers never import `google.cloud.firestore` directly.
- All data is namespaced `orgs/{orgId}/...`. There is no un-namespaced collection for application data.
- All inter-agent message publishing goes through `app/services/pubsub_client.py`'s `publish_message()` — never construct/publish a Pub/Sub message any other way. This function owns `hops` incrementing, the `hops > 12` loop cap, and deriving `requires_reply` from `act`.
- Session state is Firestore-backed via `FirestoreSessionService` (`orgs/{orgId}/agent_sessions/{agentId}`) — see `.cursor/rules/adk-conventions.mdc`.
- Every mutation that should be tamper-evident is wrapped by `@audited_task` at the department-base-class level, not called ad hoc from inside a department.
- Firestore Security Rules and backend-side membership checks are both required for any org-scoped read/write — a security rule alone is not sufficient once the backend also writes with an elevated service account.
